[0.005, "o", "\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Why did enterprise signups fall 3% in the week of 22 May 2026?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: insufficient evidence\r\nTook 97s over 8 steps, 27,316 tokens, 21 observations gathered, 16 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  The claim that enterprise signups fell 3% in the week of 22 May 2026 could not be verified: no tool available returned any data segmented by 'enterprise' tier, and the only signup series obtained (aggregate, all plans) shows no meaningful drop that week.  [posthog.event_trend cc8464c2, hubspot.contacts d5e56d93, hubspot.companies 007a62f5]\r\n  Every query scoped to enterprise, company, or deal data (HubSpot contacts/deals/companies, GA4 channel and page breakdowns) returned zero rows, and no supporting GitHub, Slack, or PostHog annotation evidence of a change or incident in this window "]
[0.000, "o", "was found either.  [hubspot.contacts d5e56d93, hubspot.search 2a1e18fa, hubspot.search 819a0e0c, hubspot.companies 007a62f5, ga4.get_sessions 619fa1e0, ga4.top_pages beea1748, github.commits d33d924d, github.commits cc202ec7, github.recent_prs 5949190c, github.issues ebe0c0bf, slack.search_messages 194891ae, slack.search_messages db3f894f, posthog.annotations 3190477c, posthog.feature_flags 1456d191]\r\n  Recommend confirming the exact enterprise-signup metric definition and re-running the investigation against a source that actually returns that segment before attributing any cause.  [posthog.event_trend cc8464c2]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  No enterprise-segmented signup data available  (medium)\r\n    - The only signup event series obtained is total 'user signed up' counts with no breakdown by plan or enterprise tier; a breakdown-by-plan request returned an unsegmented series.  [posthog.event_trend cc8464c2]\r\n  Total signups did not show a clea"]
[0.000, "o", "r 3% weekly drop  (medium)\r\n    - Total daily signups for the week of 22-28 May 2026 (25,28,27,26,25,28,27) are within the same range as the prior week (28,26,28,28,27,28,28), with no discrete drop visible in the aggregate series.  [posthog.event_trend cc8464c2]\r\n  No HubSpot company/enterprise or deal records returned for the period  (medium)\r\n    - A HubSpot contacts query for leads created 15-28 May 2026 returned zero rows.  [hubspot.contacts d5e56d93]\r\n    - A HubSpot search for contacts created in that window with a company property, a search for closed-won deals, and a companies search for 'enterprise' all returned zero rows.  [hubspot.search 2a1e18fa, hubspot.search 819a0e0c, hubspot.companies 007a62f5]\r\n  No GA4 traffic, channel, or page data returned for the window  (medium)\r\n    - GA4 total sessions by date were retrievable and showed no decline (685-715 sessions/day across 15-28 May, actually rising slightly in the week of 22 May), but a channel-group breakdown and a top-pages query for the same wi"]
[0.000, "o", "ndow both returned zero rows.  [ga4.get_sessions 1a60aac0, ga4.get_sessions 619fa1e0, ga4.top_pages beea1748]\r\n  No deploys, PRs, issues, Slack discussion, or annotations found in this window  (medium)\r\n    - GitHub commit queries against acme/product for 15-28 May and for the wider 1 May-1 June window both returned zero commits, and a pull-request and issues query for the same repo returned zero results.  [github.commits d33d924d, github.commits cc202ec7, github.recent_prs 5949190c, github.issues ebe0c0bf]\r\n    - Slack searches for 'enterprise signups' and 'signup drop' after 15 May, a PostHog annotation search for 'signup', and a PostHog feature-flag search for 'enterprise' all returned zero results.  [slack.search_messages 194891ae, slack.search_messages db3f894f, posthog.annotations 3190477c, posthog.feature_flags 1456d191]\r\n\r\nCHARTS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  user signed up over time\r\n  value\r\n    value              |▆▃▃█▅▆▅▆▃▆"]
[0.000, "o", "▆▅▆▆▁▆▅▃▁▆▅|  25 → 29\r\n                        2026-05-08 … 2026-05-28\r\n\r\n  sessions over time\r\n  sessions\r\n    sessions           |▅▂▄▃▃▅▅▇▅▇▇█▅▁|  648 → 715\r\n                        2026-05-15 … 2026-05-28\r\n\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [inconclusive] A product deploy in acme/product around 22 May caused the enterprise signup drop.\r\n      No commits, PRs, or issues were found in acme/product for either the immediate week or the full month around the date, so there is no artefact to name as a cause. This does not prove nothing shipped -- it is equally consistent with the query missing branch history -- so the hypothesis is unresolved rather than ruled out by a specific contradicting observation.\r\n  [inconclusive] A marketing traffic or channel shift reduced enterprise signups in the week of 22 May.\r\n      GA4 total sessions rose slightly in that week rather than falling, but the "]
[0.000, "o", "channel-breakdown and top-pages queries needed to attribute any change to a specific channel or page returned no rows, so this could not be tested at the segment level required.\r\n  [inconclusive] Enterprise signups specifically (as opposed to total signups) fell 3% in the week of 22 May 2026.\r\n      No tool returned data segmented by enterprise tier -- not PostHog (breakdown_property returned unsegmented), not HubSpot (all enterprise/company-scoped queries returned zero rows). The only signup series available, at the aggregate level, does not show a 3% drop in that week. The premise cannot be measured with the evidence obtained.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P1 Confirm with the analytics/RevOps team how 'enterprise signups' is defined and tracked (a specific PostHog cohort/property, a HubSpot lifecycle or company-tier filter, or a separate dashboard), then re-run this investigation against that exact definition.\r\n      why: No tool call s"]
[0.000, "o", "coped to 'enterprise' returned any rows across five different sources, which is inconsistent with a real 3% weekly movement being measurable at all -- the segment definition used in the question does not match anything queryable here.\r\n      [hubspot.contacts d5e56d93, hubspot.companies 007a62f5, posthog.feature_flags 1456d191]\r\n  P2 Do not act on the 3% figure until it is reproduced from a source that actually returns enterprise-segmented rows.\r\n      why: The aggregate signup series shows no corresponding drop in the week of 22 May, so the reported 3% cannot currently be corroborated or explained.\r\n      [posthog.event_trend cc8464c2]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Every enterprise- or company-scoped query (HubSpot contacts-with-company, HubSpot deals, HubSpot companies search, GA4 channel breakdown, GA4 top pages, GitHub commits/PRs/issues, Slack search, PostHog annotations, PostHog feature flags) returned zero rows. This pattern --"]
[0.000, "o", " uniform emptiness across unrelated sources and filters -- is more consistent with the enterprise segment, or these particular filters, not being resolvable by the tools available than with a genuine absence of enterprise activity.\r\n  - The only signup series obtained is unsegmented; a 3% move within an 'enterprise' subset averaging a small share of ~27 daily signups could easily be invisible in, or masked by, the aggregate total.\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - PostHog event_trend with breakdown_property='plan' returned an unsegmented series (breakdown_property came back null), so no plan/tier-level signup data was actually obtained despite requesting it.\r\n  - GA4 channel-group and top-pages queries for the same date range that successfully returned total sessions came back empty, suggesting a dimension or filter issue rather than a true absence of channel/page data.\r\n  - 14 of the 16 cited observation(s) returned no results (ga4.get_sessio"]
[0.000, "o", "ns, ga4.top_pages, github.commits, github.issues, github.recent_prs, hubspot.companies, hubspot.contacts, hubspot.search, posthog.annotations, posthog.feature_flags, slack.search_messages). Conclusions resting on them describe what was not found, which is not the same as what does not exist.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  1a60aac0  ga4.get_sessions  eval://ga4__get_sessions\r\n  619fa1e0  ga4.get_sessions  eval://ga4__get_sessions\r\n  beea1748  ga4.top_pages  eval://ga4__top_pages\r\n  d33d924d  github.commits  eval://github__commits\r\n  cc202ec7  github.commits  eval://github__commits\r\n  ebe0c0bf  github.issues  eval://github__issues\r\n  5949190c  github.recent_prs  eval://github__recent_prs\r\n  007a62f5  hubspot.companies  eval://hubspot__companies\r\n  d5e56d93  hubspot.contacts  eval://hubspot__contacts\r\n  2a1e18fa  hubspot.search  eval://hubspot__search\r\n  819a0e0c  hubspot.search  eval://hubspot__search\r\n  3190477c  posthog.annotations  eval://posthog"]
